      "reasons": [
        "Official ChEBI backend16196 defines cis/Z octadec9enoic acid and explicitly lists FA18:1 as ChEBI-source SYNONYM(statusC) and Octadec-9-enoic acid as ChEMBL-source SYNONYM(statusC). These are genuine recorded names, not an inferred broadMatch label copied without its predicate.",
        "Each literal is less specific than a fully stereodescriptive name. That fact alone does not establish a false synonym under §3, which allows legitimate shared names. Owner preferred Oleic acid, CAS112-80-1, cis-specific InChI and current supplier O1008 support a specific cis-oleic record. ATCC1507/173 primary OADC recipes expressly name SigmaO-1008; manufacturer captured lines84-86 identify cis aliases and lines104-106 CAS112-80-1.",
        "An ontology synonym alone would not prove a source identity; the independent original recipe/product linkage resolves this owner context. Existing evidence does not justify forcing these two names to REJECTED_LABEL solely because the strings omit position/E/Z.",
        "Recommend KEEP as existing owner-scoped names. This does not assert either string is a globally unique chemical identifier or license mapping a future unspecified FA18:1 occurrence, positional isomer, trans-isomer or salt to this owner without source assessment."
      ],
